{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sirivaḍḍha","html":"<article id='thag1.41'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.41 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.41 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Pañcamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Five </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sirivaḍḍhattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sirivaḍḍha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Vivaramanupatanti vijjutā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Lightning flashes down </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vebhārassa ca paṇḍavassa ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>on the cleft of Vebhāra and Paṇḍava. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nagavivaragato ca jhāyati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But in the mountain cleft he is absorbed in jhāna—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Putto appaṭimassa tādino”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the son of the Buddha, inimitable and unaffected. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sirivaḍḍho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
